From 077c833ba58277e73a16a13394ccc014af7f25b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:25:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Rules 4: Llama and Mistral models (ModelCfg.Arch)

ModelCfg.Arch: ArchQwen3 (0) or ArchLlama (1, Llama and Mistral: no per-head q/k RMSNorm).
Both share the stage program and weights tree; for ArchLlama the QN/KN rows are the q/k heads
as they are, and the committed q_norm/k_norm rows are never read. Llama 3.1+ rotary scaling
needs no rule: it is only a different cos/sin table in the weights tree.

MODEL_REG carries the architecture as a two-byte suffix ('A', arch) after the generation
marker, written only for ArchLlama, so earlier registrations encode, decode and hash into the
state root exactly as before. Registering an ArchLlama model needs Rules 4 (no network
schedules Rules 4 yet). Tests: referee vs the Python runtime on a tiny Llama fixture
(testdata/llama_tiny.json.gz), wire format, activation, state root.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Li1NuzogEfSRnjn3KNzFm
